00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.380
from Comic-Con@Home,

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.290
a panel centered around Zack Snyder

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.230
revealed some pretty interesting details

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:27.720
about his version of "Justice League,"

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.640
which is coming to HBO Max next year.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.760
Counting down the days.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.110
And he debuted a never-before-seen clip

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.800
that features Henry Cavill's Superman

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.920
wearing the black suit
while meeting Alfred,

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.800
played by, of course, Jeremy Irons.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.580
A lot of star power in one scene.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.800
- Well, that was fun while it didn't last.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.130
- Now, basically the black suit

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.760
dates back to the comics in the '90s,

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.270
when a pretty huge deal was
made about the death of Superman

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.110
at the hands of Doomsday,
which is also who killed him

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.190
in "Batman v Superman: Dawn of justice."

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.500
But when he inevitably
returned in the comics,

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.030
he initially wore a black
version of his iconic suit,

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.190
which has since become a
popular piece of Superman lore.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:06.030
Also, most of us just look
better in black anyway, right?

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.500
So it was thought that when
Superman was resurrected

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.350
in "Justice League," we would see it,

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.660
which Snyder has said was his
intention from the beginning.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:15.080
So, in other words, it looks like

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.673
we'll be getting more of
Superman's resurrection story.

00:01:17.673 --> 00:01:20.120
♪ Hallelujah ♪

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:21.380
Of course his original version

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.020
was drastically changed by
new director Joss Whedon

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:25.870
after Snyder left the project -

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.910
and for more on that,
check out our past episodes

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:29.220
about the Snyder Cut -

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.310
meaning we did not see the black suit

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.900
in the version that exists right now,

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:36.227
which is a Rotten 40% on
the Tomatometer, by the way.

00:01:36.227 --> 00:01:37.329
- Ride ain't over yet.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:38.500
- My man!

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.100
