00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.530
was actually in a deleted scene

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.780
that came with the "Justice
League" Blu-ray release.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:44.730
Remember those?

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.450
And in it, we see Clark Kent
in the fortress of solitude,

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.150
walking past both the black suit

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.040
and some Kryptonian space armor.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.570
Can we talk about how dope
that closet was, though?

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.730
Funny enough, that scene
could have really helped

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:57.730
Superman's character
arc in "Justice League,"

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:58.890
which is one of the many reasons

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:01.725
fans have demanded to see a Snyder Cut.

00:02:01.725 --> 00:02:04.790
- Good. 'Cause I really like being alive.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:07.360
- Speaking of which, Snyder
also teased on the panel

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.187
that he is trying to secure the name

00:02:09.187 --> 00:02:11.470
"Zack Snyder's Justice
League" for the film,

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:13.770
but isn't sure if that's legally possible.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.970
Would love your thoughts on that one.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.230
And the clip that was shown

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:18.950
shows off one of his main focuses,

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.800
which is restoring the
film's intended aspect ratio,

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.820
